---
// src/components/ui/HeroScatterDecoration.astro
// Purely decorative scattered-dot layer, designed as a companion to the
// floating AutomationNotificationCard set — not a second competing
// "background pattern" alongside Hero.astro's cloud-blur glow.
// The cloud-blur is atmosphere (sits behind everything); this layer is a
// foreground prop of small dots scattered across the hero, mixing with the
// gradient rather than clustering strictly at the corners.
//
// DESIGN SYSTEM NOTE (per CLAUDE.md Section 4.5 — Per-Page
// Inspiration-Driven Design): scoped to this component/hero only; does not
// change the sitewide illustration guidance in DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Section 7/7.5.
//
// Colors: dots use the three approved accent/signal tokens (blue-600,
// teal-600, amber-500) — no new hex values introduced. Size (small/medium/
// large) and opacity are varied per-dot so each stays legible against
// whatever part of the gradient it lands on; nothing here is an inline
// style="..." attribute, per the standing zero-tolerance rule — all
// variation is expressed through Tailwind utility classes and arbitrary
// bracket values under the decorative-transform exception in CLAUDE.md
// Section 3.
//
// TEXT-COLUMN CLEARANCE (this pass): Hero.astro centers its headline/
// paragraph content in a `max-w-2xl` (672px) column with no max-width on
// the `<section>` itself. This layer only renders at `lg:` and up (see
// Hero.astro's `class="hidden lg:block"` on this component), so the
// narrowest viewport it ever appears on is 1024px — at that width the
// centered column already spans from ~17% to ~83% horizontally, and that
// safe-zone-for-text only gets wider (not narrower) on bigger screens.
// Every dot below is kept at ≤15% from the left or right edge so none of
// them can ever land inside the text column at any `lg`+ width, while
// still landing well outside the four original corner positions.
//
// FIXED-HEADER CLEARANCE FIX (this pass): this wrapper was `absolute
// inset-0`, which stretches it to the parent `<section>`'s full box
// starting at the section's own top edge (y=0 inside the section) —
// completely ignoring the section's `pt-40/sm:pt-48/lg:pt-56` padding,
// since padding only affects in-flow children, not `inset-0` absolutely-
// positioned ones. That let the top-[%] dots calculate their position
// from a box that started above/behind Nav.astro's fixed header, same
// root cause as the corner-card wrapper in Hero.astro. Swapped `inset-0`
// for explicit `top-40 sm:top-48 lg:top-56 inset-x-0 bottom-0` — same
// clearance values as the section's own top padding — so this layer's
// box now starts exactly where the section's padded content area starts,
// and every dot's top-[%]/bottom-[%] value keeps the same relative
// position within the hero it always had. Dot content, sizes, colors,
// opacities, and every individual top/left/right/bottom percentage below
// are untouched.
//
// BOTTOM-EDGE COUNTERPART FIX (this pass): the wrapper's `bottom-0` had
// the same bug as the old `inset-0` top edge, just on the other side —
// it stretched to the section's true bottom edge, ignoring the section's
// own `pb-28 sm:pb-40` bottom padding. That made the box these dots'
// bottom-[%] values are calculated against taller than intended, pulling
// bottom-anchored dots down closer to the section's real bottom edge
// than the top-anchored dots sit from the top — a visible top/bottom
// asymmetry. Swapped `bottom-0` for `bottom-28 sm:bottom-40`, mirroring
// the section's own bottom padding exactly like `top-40 sm:top-48
// lg:top-56` mirrors its top padding. Box is now symmetric on both
// edges; individual dot percentages untouched.

export interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;

// ⚠️ Flag (per CLAUDE.md Section 3 "stop and flag" rule): this pass
// replaces the previous 3-accent-color dot scatter with a white/paper-
// toned starfield (per direct request — "dots" → "stars in the sky").
// text-paper/white shades are NOT one of DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's three
// approved signal/accent colors (blue-600/teal-600/amber-500); used here
// because a starfield reads as white/silver by definition against the
// dark bg-ink hero. Confirm with design before shipping, or restyle with
// an approved accent tint if that's preferred.
//
// Star field: ~26 stars total, mixing tiny/small/medium sizes and a
// spread of opacities so it reads as depth (some stars faint/far, some
// bright/near) rather than a flat repeated dot. A handful carry a
// `.star-twinkle` class (staggered animation-delay via inline style is
// avoided per the zero-tolerance rule — delay is instead varied through
// distinct utility classes .star-twinkle-a/b/c below) for subtle
// movement so the sky doesn't feel static. Unlike the old dot layer,
// stars are scattered across the FULL width (not just ≤15% from each
// edge) since a sky plausibly has stars behind/around the headline too —
// but density is kept low directly behind the text column and opacity
// is kept low there, so contrast against the headline/subtext is
// preserved.
---

<div class:list={['pointer-events-none top-40 sm:top-48 lg:top-56 inset-x-0 bottom-28 sm:bottom-40 absolute -z-[5]', className]}
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <!-- Bright/near stars (larger, higher opacity, some twinkling).
       CONTRAST PASS (this pass): opacities retuned per-star based on
       proximity to the gradient's brightest zone (top-center, where
       Hero.astro's radial wash is strongest) vs. the darker ink zone
       (edges/lower half, widened this same pass — see Hero.astro's own
       gradient comment). Stars sitting near top-center are dimmed so
       they don't wash out against the bright blue; stars near edges/
       bottom are brightened since they now sit against genuinely dark
       ink and can afford more presence. Positions, sizes, and which
       stars twinkle are untouched — only bg-paper/NN opacity values
       changed below. -->
  <span class="star-twinkle-a absolute left-[18%] top-[14%] h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-paper/85"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-b absolute right-[22%] top-[10%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/60"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-c absolute bottom-[16%] left-[24%] h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-paper/90"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-a absolute bottom-[10%] right-[18%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/95"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-b absolute left-[9%] top-[42%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/90"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-c absolute right-[9%] top-[60%] h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-paper/85"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-a absolute left-[13%] bottom-[38%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/90"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-b absolute right-[13%] bottom-[24%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/85"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-c absolute left-[35%] top-[8%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/35"></span>
  <span class="star-twinkle-a absolute right-[38%] top-[18%] h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-paper/45"></span>

  <!-- Small/mid-distance stars, static, opacity retuned this pass on
       the same bright-zone/dark-zone logic as the twinkling stars
       above. -->
  <span class="absolute left-[28%] top-[24%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/40"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[30%] top-[34%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/50"></span>
  <span class="absolute left-[45%] top-[16%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/25"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[44%] top-[8%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/20"></span>
  <span class="absolute left-[6%] top-[20%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/70"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[6%] top-[26%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/65"></span>
  <span class="absolute left-[20%] bottom-[6%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/65"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[24%] bottom-[8%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/70"></span>
  <span class="absolute left-[16%] top-[52%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/60"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[16%] top-[48%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/60"></span>
  <span class="absolute left-[38%] bottom-[14%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/45"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[40%] bottom-[18%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/45"></span>

  <!-- Faint/far stars — central band stars (closest to the gradient's
       brightest zone) kept the faintest; the two lower-center stars sit
       in the now-widened dark zone so were nudged up slightly from the
       previous pass. -->
  <span class="absolute left-[48%] top-[30%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/15"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[48%] top-[40%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/20"></span>
  <span class="absolute left-[42%] bottom-[28%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/30"></span>
  <span class="absolute right-[42%] bottom-[32%] h-0.5 w-0.5 rounded-full bg-paper/30"></span>
</div>

<style>
  /* Twinkle keyframes — three variants with different durations/delays
     (staggered via distinct classes, not inline style, per the
     zero-tolerance rule) so twinkling stars don't all pulse in unison. */
  @keyframes star-twinkle {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 0.35; transform: scale(0.85); }
    50% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.15); }
  }
  .star-twinkle-a { animation: star-twinkle 3.2s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .star-twinkle-b { animation: star-twinkle 4s ease-in-out infinite 0.8s; }
  .star-twinkle-c { animation: star-twinkle 2.6s ease-in-out infinite 1.4s; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .star-twinkle-a, .star-twinkle-b, .star-twinkle-c {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
